# Crewbase Collective — project context

Before changing code, read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root (single source of truth shared with Claude Code).
For a plain-language overview read `docs/SIMPLE_GUIDE.md`; for what each file does read `docs/CODE_MAP.md`.

Key rules (full list in AGENTS.md):
- Content = JSON files in `data/` (source of truth). `client/public/data/` and `client/public/images/` are generated by `npm run build:data` — never edit by hand.
- Admin screens live in `client/src/pages/admin/` (the `cms/` app just routes to them). The CMS runs locally only and has no login — never deploy it.
- Production API (`server/src/app.ts`) only handles `/api/health`, `/api/subscribe`, `/api/requests`. No content CRUD there.
- Schema lives in `server/src/data/types.ts`. Admin-only fields (person email/phone/notes/roles, event `associated`) must never be written to public JSON.
- `server/src/db/`, `auth.ts`, `upload.ts`, `routes/admin.ts`, `routes/public.ts` are legacy Postgres code — don't extend them.
